    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d520-a1">

                <pb facs="0811" n="683" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg683"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 305.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Igúzquia to Mr. McKay</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of Spain</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Key West,
                                Fla.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1885-01-14"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 14,
                    1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: In reply to your favor of this date,
                    in which you inquire whether I have reported to my Government the amount of the
                    fees collected by this consulate on neat cattle shipped in past years in
                    American vessels to the island of Cuba, I hasten to inform <pb facs="0812"
                        n="684" xml:id="pg684"/> you that, in obedience to orders received, I sent,
                    under date of December 20, 1884, to his excellency the minister of state of His
                    Majesty, a general statement of those fees which had been improperly collected,
                    by mistake, and, also, of the amounts which are to be returned to the interested
                    parties, in pursuance of the royal order.</p>
                <p>I take pleasure, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRANCO. FERNANDEZ IGUZQUIA.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
